This '''timeline of major events''' attempts to lay out the most important points in history leading up to the [[Second Renaissance]]. All dates are in Earth Standard Dating.

==[[21st Century]]==
===[[Great Reset]]===
{| class="wikitable"
|-
| 2026
| '''[[The Flood]]''': The South Greenland Ice Sheet falls into the Atlantic devastating coastal cities and sending sea levels 7 meters above pre-Anthropocene levels. By August, Hurricane Julia strikes the Eastern Seaboard, destroying the hastily constructed levees and sea walls. The United States capital city is temporarily relocated to Columbus until the completion of the new DC Sea Wall two years later.
|-
| 2025-2027
| '''Labor Shortage''': Retirement of the Baby Boomers begins to peak, opening up millions of jobs for Millenials and Centennials (Generation Z). The developed world reaches full employment as additional jobs open up to not only replace but to support the elderly. The new demand for labor produces a competitive wage economy, but heightened inflation reduces overall buying power.
|-
| 2024-2032
| '''[[Great Famine|Famine]]''': Ocean desalination due to the Flood devastates fish populations, while rising tides and [[Revolutions of 2027|social unrest around the world]] causes catastrophic supply chain interruptions to agriculture. A worldwide famine sets in that kills millions. Economic and social unrest leads to political upheavals across the world leading to civil war in [[Second Chinese Civil War| China]]. To the southwest, Pakistan and the already devastated Afghan state would fragment. And in Western Europe, states such as Germany and France would hold new elections and calls for constitutional referendums.
|-
|2026
|'''[[Timeline of space exploration|Humans on Mars]]''': The [[Mars Corporation]] launches its first manned mission to [[Mars]]. Meridian Base is established. Bradbury Base is established in lower Tharsis shortly thereafter.
|-
| 2027-2032
| '''[[Market Crash of 2027]]''': The global economy continues to stagnate as the demand for labor leaves the housing and financial sectors of the global economy in ruins. Home prices drop to record lows and investor confidence is in shatters as there is no clear way for companies to keep up with the demand for goods. Inflation leaves most major currencies on their knees, and people are left working full time, with high wages, and have nothing to spend it on.
|-
| 2028-2031
| '''[[White Tide]]''': The influx of domestic climate refugees into once-rural communities and the election of [[Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez]] leads to a wave of White Nationalist insurrections in the United States.
|-
|2029-2038
|'''[[Dissolution of the Russian Federation]]''': [[North Atlantic Treaty Organization|NATO]] and [[United Nations|UN]] forces make incursions into the former Russian Federation to secure nuclear stockpiles from breakaway republics and rogue generals. Some states such as [[Buryatia]] and [[Tuva]] voluntarily hand over their stockpiles, while [[Primorye]], the [[Ural Republic]], Samara, and the future [[Russia|Russian Republic]] refuse to surrender their weapons but such states were unwilling to utilize these weapons in fear of nuclear retaliation from other nuclear powers. For the next 9 years, international forces engage in a series of wars to secure former Russian nuclear weapons. [[Poland]] and [[Turkey]] divide their respective spheres of influence in Russia through the [[Treaty of Odessa]].
|-
| 2029-2035
| '''[[Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez|Immigration Reform]]''': The US Government enacts a new series of Immigration reform policies, taking advantage of the refugee crisis. Millions of Burmese, Thai, Vietnamese, Nigerian, Chinese, Indian, and Bengali immigrants flooded into North America as their home countries drowned, driving the United States population to 400 million citizens.
|-
| 2025-2030
| '''Rise of Turkey''': Turkey begins a prolonged occupation of Arabia after the fall of the Islamic State and US disengagement from the Middle East. Over the next decade Turkish power expands to every corner of the Middle East and even into southern Russia. The Turks use infrastructure to consolidate their power, building the largest oil pipeline in history, stretching from the Arctic to the Bosporus.
|-
| 2030-2038
| '''Exploration of the Outer Planets''': Galileo Development is founded from within LE. The company launches the largest spacecraft in history, the Galileo II to the Jovian system to develop it for resources. By 2036 the first expedition reaches Saturn and establishes the Gondor Colony on Titan. Regular deliveries of Nitrogen from Titan to Mars begin in 2038.
|-
| 2029-2037
| '''[[Seventh Party System|American Renewal]]''': The US government spends trillions on new social services to elevate the inflation crisis and attract new immigrants to the US. Millions of suburban houses are seized by the government and replaced with new urban civil works programs. Medicare is extended to every citizen in the United States. Private retirement programs are completely replaced by Social Security. Much of the developed world digitizes their currency to better control inflation. 
|}
