===[[Space Age]]===
{| class="wikitable"
|-
|2039-2048
|'''Japanese Resurgence''': [[Japan]] establishes a series of Extraterritorial Districts in Chita and Kamchatka to service the millions of displaced peoples from their population. The country demonstrates its first [[Hypersonic weapon|hypersonic weapon]] in 2039. In response, the US begins supporting nationalist movements in China and Taiwan to guard against the Japanese and Turks.
|-
| 2039-2049
| '''[[The Flood#Increased rate of melting|Antarctic Flood]]''': Additional melt off in Antarctica drives greater increases in sea levels to 30 meters above pre-Anthropocene levels. Temperatures peak at around 3 degrees Celsius above pre-Anthropocene levels. Most sea walls hold until the [[The Flood#Summer of Storms|2043 Hurricane Season]], which leaves many of the world's last remaining sea walls destroyed. The damage to the British Isles drives millions of British and Irish citizens to flee for North America. Two years later, the British Parliament votes to dissolve the Monarchy and take direct possession of their lands to deal with the loss of so much of their critical territory. In Canada, the First Nations use the increased traffic through the Arctic to gain independence. Germany and France formally annex the remaining territories of Belgium and Netherlands not swallowed by the sea.
|-
|2045
|'''Rise of Poland''': Poland's sphere of influence grows as Slovenia and Croatia join the Visegrad group.
|-
|2045-2051
|'''[[Earth Working Group]]''': The Earth Working Group is established by consortium of businesses, NGOs and governments to to reverse the effects of climate change in 2045. Two years later, The Earth Working Group begins digging out ancient lake and river basins in the Sahara. Self-assembled aqueducts are constructed by the Working Group to begin draining excess seawater into the new man-made lakes of Africa and Central Asia. Excess sand and rock are used to construct hills around the world's new lake and river basins to shield them from wind erosion. Trees, shrubs, and grasses are planted to sustain a hydrological cycle in the Sahara.
|-
| 2049
| '''[[Balkan Crisis]]''': Turkey formally absorbs the Caucasus by 2049. Poland protests and mobilizes troops. Turkey positions its forces in Bosnia on high alert bringing the planet to the brink of War.
|-
| 2051-2055
| '''[[World War III]]''': Japan stages a massive attack on US space and air forces while Turkey invades the Balkans and Russia. In the face of global war, the [[United Nations]] dissolves.
|-
|2054
|'''East Africa''': East Africa unites in anticipation of the massive quantities of wealth that are about to flow into their lands from the stars.
|-
|2058
|'''Reunification of China''': Mainland China and Taiwan reunite as the [[United Federation of China]].
|-
| 2058-2061
| '''Project Prometheus''': NASA is given a budget infusion. Research on Warp Drive conducted during the war accelerates the completion of [[Prometheus 1]], the first spacecraft capable of faster-than-light travel. Launched to Alpha Centauri, the interstellar probe succeeds in proving the practical application of the White-Alcubierre Drive, and delivers a wealth of new information on an [[Atlantis (planet)|Earthlike planet around Alpha Centauri B.]]
|-
|2058
|'''DC Reconstruction''': The New DC Sea Wall is torn down and reconstruction of the old portions of the city begins.
|-
|2061-2071
|'''[[Augment Rights Movement]]''': Human augmentation technology developed during the Third World War leads to a new generation of veterans and retirees who are able to return to life in a better state than they left it. In 2065, student groups march on Washington DC to protest the Falana Act, claiming banning recreational augmentations is a violation to their right to freedom of expression. Five years later, law enforcement agencies are barred from discriminating against augmented humans when hiring. The following year, the [[Augment Rights Act]] is passed.
|-
| 2064
| '''First Contact''': Launch of the first warp ship with a White-Alcubierre drive, the ISV Enterprise. The ship is stocked for a seven year mission to explore nearby star systems. It reaches the Alpha-Centauri system in two weeks. The crew of the Enterprise makes first contact with the [[K'lerin]] of [[Le'ma|Tau Ceti f]].
|-
|2054-2065
|'''[[The Refreeze]]''': Martian mirrors are placed in Polar Orbit to reduce global temperatures and rebuild arctic glaciers. The northwest passage is closed with Ice by 2063 and Sea Levels return to pre-Anthropocene heights. Reconstruction of the previously flooded regions begins. The closure of the Northwest Passage and environmental impact on the [[Arctic states]] leads to [[Winter Recession|the worst recession in 40 years.]]
|-
|2064-2073
|'''[[First Nations War]]''': In 2064, conflict erupts between Canada, Quebec, and the First Nations. The United States intervenes in the Canadian Civil War and deploys forces to prevent the spread of the conflict from hurt American interests. In 2067, the Canadian Civil War ends with a ceasefire. Canada is occupied by the United States. Six years later, the [[Union Act of 2073|Union Act]] is passed, formally annexing the British Isles, Canada, the former First Nations, Australia, and New Zealand into the United States.
|-
| 2070
| '''New Age of Exploration''': The Enterprise returns to Earth, a dozen other starships are now exploring the Local Bubble. Colonization via W-A Drive is not practical, due to the limits of W-A field volume.
|-
|2070
|[[Proclamation of Sapere aude|'''Proclamation of Sapere aude''']]: Pope Francis II issues the Proclamation of Sapere aude, outlining a series of major reforms to the Catholic Church that originated in the [[Fifth Great Awakening|progressive chapters in the United States]].
|-
|2070-2075
|'''Automation''': AutoProgramming software begins placing millions of programmers out of work. By 2075, unemployment reaches 27% in the United States as automated systems begin outmoding technical jobs such as programming, architecture, and a number of engineering positions.
|-
| 2079-2081
| '''[[First Martian Revolution]]''': On the eve of [[Mars]] being opened for large scale human colonization, the space economy stands on the edge of collapse at the threat of the United States government closing its borders. The First Martian Revolution ends with the Rosalind Amendment. Establishing a line of legal separation between the United States on Earth and the space colonies, that essentially makes them semi-autonomous territories. Following the First Martian Revolution, the Mars Corporation official dissolves, and formal territorial governments are established with the [[Interplanetary Trade Commission]] serving as an administrative entity.
|-
| 2078-2084
| '''[[Second Depression]]''': A massive global recession resulting from rising effective demand and a growing robotic workforce that contributed to mass layoffs.
|}
